  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Populated Board",
    "overview": "The page is a fabricated printed circuit board. A 3D print lays it down layer by layer (substrate, copper, component bodies), the camera settles straight down, and the materials flatten to the exact page colours so the print becomes the page with no seam. From then on every surface is board material: matte black solder mask for ground, ENIG gold copper for every line, pad and via, silkscreen off-white for every word, and one red SMD LED for the one thing to do.\n\nDensity is low and deliberate. Type is very large and very condensed, rows are separated by wide section gaps, and the board itself is the only dense area: a central MCU wired by 45-degree copper to one component per role. Photographs are of the material world the work lives in, always greyscale, so colour stays reserved for copper and the LED. Motion is fabrication: toolpath wipes left to right, traces drawn along their length, signal pulses travelling to a part. Nothing bounces and nothing fades in for decoration alone.\n\nDark ground and the red accent are product commitments, not choices this world can revisit.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Matte black mask ground with a single green-black raised step; no gradients, no glass.",
      "Copper is the only line colour: rules, bullets, underlines, traces, vias, figures.",
      "LED red only for the email action and whatever is lit; one lit component at a time on the board.",
      "Square rectangles everywhere; circles appear only as vias, mounting holes and fiducials.",
      "Archivo variable: heavy condensed display (wdth 74-76), normal-width text (wdth 100).",
      "Motion as deposition: wipes, drawn traces, pulses; strong ease-out, no bounce."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The LED Means On Rule",
        "body": "LED red is only ever the email action or a part that is lit (the active component, a status LED, the reply LED, the boat on its route). It is never decoration, emphasis or a status colour for text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Copper Line Rule",
        "body": "Every non-type line on the page is copper (or dim copper). No grey hairlines, no silk rules; the BOM table's dark row rule is the single exception, because it is a printed table.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Hand-off Rule",
        "body": "The print intro's `flat` material colours equal these tokens exactly. Change a token, change config/print-config.ts in the same commit.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Five Steps Rule",
        "body": "Five sizes, no more: display, title, lead, body, small. Emphasis comes from weight and width, not new sizes.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Silkscreen Case Rule",
        "body": "Type is set in sentence case at normal tracking. No uppercase labels, no small tracked headers above headings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Layer Not Lift Rule",
        "body": "Separate surfaces with a mask tone step or copper, never with a shadow or blur.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do reserve LED red for the email action and lit parts; light one board component at a time.",
      "Do draw every non-type line in copper or dim copper, with 45-degree routing and round caps.",
      "Do separate surfaces with mask tone steps (mask, mask-raised, mask-deep) rather than shadows.",
      "Do set headings heavy and condensed (weight 800-820, wdth 74-76) and running text at full width.",
      "Do show photographs greyscale (grayscale 1, contrast 1.08, brightness 0.86) and credit them.",
